ing otherwise            in modern Lahu, and is closely homophonous with P^ (V) 'die' and P6            (N) 'blood', the name of this day is folk-etymologized as ch^-ni by            many speakers, thus introducing into the cycle a new and familiar            animal with positive connotations/     ch^-p1-ch^-ma  (Elabn)        male and female barking-deer     ch^=pI-qwS\  (N)              barking-deer          /the usual BL term/          ch%=pI-qwS\ tI qo G-k^ mZ cG /  The barking-deer has no gall-                                   bladder.               /an (erroneous) explanation of why the animal is timid/          ch^=pI-qwS\_lO(n)  (N)   black barking-deer; Fea's barking deer                                    [Muntiacus feae]               /SYN. dA=ch^-@ (N)/     ch^-pX  (N)                   night wasp (species about an inch long, the                                    color of a barking-deer)     ch^=phu-q1  (N)               a barking-deer buckch^  (V)                           weigh (sthg)     /< PLB *kyi:n1 (cf. WB khyin) < PTB *ki:n [STC #369]; cf. hB (Vadj)/     n1-nZ\ ch^ ve  (OV)           measure the weight          /n1-nZ\ < Thai nQm-nAk 'weight'/          qhA-ma hB ve n1-nZ\ ch^ ve  (OV)  see how much sthg weighs ("measure                                             the weight of how heavy it is")     phu ch^ 1 ve  (Nrh + RRC)     weighed silver     ch^-tu  (N)                   a balance; scale          ch^-tu=P8  (N)           weights (for a balance)               /SYNS. mA\-cwS=P8 (N), y1-c7=P8 (N)/          ch^-tu=ywX  (N)          a kind of balance     y1-c7 ch^ ve  (Nspec + V)     weigh with a scale; weigh in a balancech^  (Clf)                         four annas of silver (= 1/4 rupee); 25 pya                                    (= 1/4 of a Burmese kyat)     /prob. same etymon as ch^ (V)/     phu n< ch^  (NPq)             8 annas